          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/xci-U7ZdRXe7lXRdChF0Zif_8ssRu3YIYB-Xod2l9_jlSNlh8jwcVoZweiwzVmwHqQraVWJ6OZM=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "​@upfront653 Generally, yes. Mingolia is a constitutional democratic republic. Citizens have legally protected freedoms such as freedom of speech, religion, peaceful assembly, and movement, although—as in other countries—these freedoms are subject to laws and limitations.\n\nFor a visitor, this means you can generally travel around the country, interact with people, practice your religion, take photographs, and live your daily life without needing special permission beyond complying with ordinary laws and immigration requirements.\n\nCan foreigners stay for a long time?\nYes. This is one of the things that makes Mongolia attractive to long-term visitors.\n\nFor many nationalities that qualify for visa-free entry, the initial tourist stay is 30 days. The Bureau of Immigration allows an initial 29-day extension, and further extensions can be obtained under the applicable visitor-visa rules.",
